BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Underground Film Series: BEAUTY AND THE BEAST
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261114T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261114T210000
UID:1bf78ef5f212ccb89893a016c9e03a44@wfhb.org
DESCRIPTION:Gorgeously shot\, intriguingly surreal\, and thrillingly sensu
 al\, this Czech retelling of the beloved fairytale is unlike any adaptatio
 n before or since. The most uncanny and fierce adaptation of Beauty and th
 e Beast \, the film follows the innocent Julie and her experiences living 
 under the watchful eye of Netvor\, a bird-like being torn between his grow
 ing affection for her and his animalistic urge to kill. Directed by Juraj 
 Herz of the Czech New Wave\, Herz masterfully infuses the 18th-century Fre
 nch fairytale of impossible affection with the aesthetics of gothic horror
 . Restored by Národní filmový archiv\, Prague and Severin Films\, suppo
 rted by The Czech Audiovisual Fund. [91 min\; horror\, fantasy\; Czech wit
 h English subtitles]
LOCATION:IU Cinema\, 1213 E. Seventh Street \, Bloomington
URL:https://wfhb.org/events/underground-film-series-beauty-and-the-beast/
X-SOURCE:WFHB Community Calendar
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“Idomeneo” by Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261114T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20261114T213000
UID:b0c86b80ad3c093b4002841217bd16cf@wfhb.org
DESCRIPTION:After King Idomeneo returns to Crete from the Trojan War\, the
  high-stakes consequences of a desperate deal he struck with Neptune for s
 afe passage reveal themselves when he must choose between his own son\, Id
 amante\, and the vow he made to the sea god\, further complicated as Idama
 nte is loved by both the Trojan princess Ilia and the jealous Greek prince
 ss Elettra. But when divine wrath is incurred\, Idamante and Ilia prove th
 eir worth\, prompting Neptune’s mercy. NB: Opera Insights: Pre-show talk
  on Mozart’s “Idomeneo” – Presented by Peyson Weekley in the Music
 al Arts Center Lobby at 6:30.
LOCATION:IU Musical Arts Center\, 101 North Eagleson Avenue\,  Bloomington
 \, IN
URL:https://wfhb.org/events/idomeneo-by-wolfgang-amadeus-mozart/
X-SOURCE:WFHB Community Calendar
END:VEVENT
